izations\nUndergraduate Students\nStudent Groups\nSociety of Physics Students\nWe Belong in Physics\nCourse Listing\nScholarships\nPhysics Tutoring\nDegree Requirements\nStudent Resources\nCareer Resources\nColloquia and Seminars\nAccelerated Master\u2019s Programs\nUndergraduate Research\nGraduate Students\nGraduate School Forms\nFAQ\nPhysics Graduate Courses\nGraduate Degree Plans\nResources and Perks\nCareer Resources\nColloquia and Seminars\nFaculty & Staff\nResources and Perks\nColloquia and Seminars\nTravel Resources\nKuali Resources\nAlumni & Friends\nHistory\nDepartment Photos\nHistorical Articles\nFuture Grad Students\nICARUS collaboration at Fermilab\nLearn More\nThe Department of Physics at Colorado State University is home to 22 faculty members who maintain research programs in Atomic and Molecular Optics Physics, Condensed Matter Physics, High-Energy Particle Physics and Particle Astrophysics, and Theoretical Physics. The CSU Physics Department\u2019s strength is the friendly and individualized relationship between students and faculty.\nGraduate students in the department will take part in research programs and with teaching in the undergraduate laboratories. As part of their research, students will take significant and leading roles in some of the most exciting areas of physics. Incoming students may enter the program interested in several fields and explore the different experimental and theoretical possibilities within the department before deciding their own research path.\nThe application deadline for full consideration for Fall admissions is January 15th. Applications received after the deadline will be considered as they come in until all positions are filled.\nPlease note:\nBeginning in January 2026, the TOEFL scoring scale will transition to a 1-6. Existing TOEFL scores will continue to be valid for two years. You can find more information regarding English Proficiency requirements here: https://graduateschool.colostate.edu/admissions-resources/english-proficiency/\nWe strive to minimize the financial costs of applying.\nMany applicants will qualify for automatic fee waivers or can request fee waivers. See https://graduateschool.colostate.edu/skip-the-application-fee/ for information on fee waivers.\nOfficial transcripts and official test scores are only required upon admission.\nContact our Graduate Student Coordinator at: Physics_Grad_Admissions@mail.colostate.edu or (970) 491-6207.\nFAQ\nHow Do I Apply?\nDegree Program\nVisiting Campus\nBecome a Ram today\nApply Now\nSingle Atom Detection, Quantum Computing Lab\nWe're active in the community\nEngagement\nCSU Photon Detectors\nAstronomy\nINTERESTED IN Physics? TALK TO US\nContact Info\nLittle Shop of Physics\nWhat are we up to?\nResearch Areas\nDepartment of Physics\nAR124 Engineering Building\n1875 Campus Delivery\nFort Collins, Colorado 80523-1875\nIn-Office Hours:\nMon - Fri 8:00am - 4:30pm\nTelephone: 970-491-6206\nEmail: physics_reception@Mail.Colostate.edu\nCollege of Natural Sciences\nContact Details\nwww.natsci.colostate.edu\nDepartments\nBiochemistry & Molecular Biology\nBiology\nChemistry\nComputer Science\nMathematics\nPhysics\nPsychology\nStatistics\nSupport the College\nGIVE NOW\nContact CSU\nApply to CSU\nAccessibility Statement\nDisclaimer\nEqual Opportunity\nPrivacy Statement\n\u00a9 Colorado State University - College of Natural Sciences, Fort Collins, CO 80523", "links": [["Colorado State University", "https://colostate.edu"], ["College of Natural Sciences", "https://www.natsci.colostate.edu"], ["Department of Physics", "https://www.physics.colostate.edu/"], ["About", "https://www.physics.colostate.edu/about/"], ["People", "https://www.physics.colostate.edu/about/people/"], ["Affiliate Faculty and Guest Associates in Research", "https://www.physics.colostate.edu/about/affiliate-faculty/"], ["Contact Info", "https://www.physics.colostate.edu/about/contact-info/"], ["Astronomy", "https://www.physics.colostate.edu/about/astronomy/"], ["L